{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then v_2 ≠ "sum" ∧ v_2 ≠ "prod" ∧ v_2 ≠ "min" ∧ v_2 ≠ "max"
>>
Rule 100 (if the tensor has 2 dimensions, and message is not none, sum of the shape values has to be greater than the message length squared.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2 ≠ "none" then shape(v_1, 0) + shape(v_1, 1) > v_2.len * v_2.len
>>
Rule 101 (When input is of type int32 and int64 then message has to be smaller than 5 char.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4) then v_2.len < 5
>>
Rule 102 (If tensor dimension is > 2 and type is complex, the max and min must differ by at least 0.1.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10) ∧ ndim(v_1) > 2 then (max(v_1) - min(v_1)) > 0.1
>>
Rule 103 (If input tensor has one dimension the string message must start with letter l or v.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then (v_2[0] = "l" ∨ v_2[0] = "v")
>>
Rule 104 (When the dimension is 3 and datatype is float32, then all the shape has to be at least 2.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 7) ∧ ndim(v_1) = 3 then shape(v_1, 0) >= 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) >= 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) >= 2
>>
Rule 105 (If a message is specified, the product of all dimensions should be greater or equal to the length of the message)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if v_2.len > 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i)) ≥ v_2.len
>>
Rule 106 (Message must be smaller than 3 if the tensor is of boolean type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then v_2.len < 3
>>
Rule 107 (For a tensor with dimension > 3, the average cannot be equal the min or the max)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 3 then (max(v_1) > min(v_1))
